# Docker socket – use socket-proxy only

Any service that needs the Docker API (Traefik, Diun, Dockge, Portainer, etc.) must **not** mount `/var/run/docker.sock` directly. Use the **socket-proxy** instead.

- **Traefik:** `--providers.docker.endpoint=tcp://socket-proxy:2375` (no socket volume).
- **Diun:** `DIUN_PROVIDERS_DOCKER_ENDPOINT=tcp://socket-proxy:2375` (no socket volume).
- **Dockge / Portainer / others:** `DOCKER_HOST=tcp://socket-proxy:2375` (no socket volume).

The service must be on the **backends** network so it can reach `socket-proxy:2375`. Only the `socket-proxy` container may mount `/var/run/docker.sock`.

```yaml
# ❌ BAD – direct socket mount in app
volumes:
  - /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock

# ✅ GOOD – use proxy
environment:
  - DOCKER_HOST=tcp://socket-proxy:2375
# and no docker.sock volume
```
